# Complete Text-to-Image Generation Model: Full Implementation Specification in Zig

## Objective

Construct a production-ready text-to-image and image-to-image generation model from scratch using Zig programming language. The system must implement nine advanced techniques from recent research (2024-2026) and achieve competitive quality with state-of-the-art models. The implementation will use Zig 0.12+, custom CUDA kernels for GPU acceleration, and deploy on Modal.com infrastructure with B200 GPU access.

## System Architecture Overview

The model consists of five primary modules implemented entirely in Zig:

1. Text Encoder (GLM-4-9B reimplemented in Zig with Riemannian projection)
2. Latent Space (Riemannian manifold with wavelet decomposition)
3. Dense Associative Memory Layer (Hopfield networks)
4. Generative Pipeline (Rectified flow with two-stage refinement)
5. VAE Decoder (Equivariance-aware reconstruction)

Total trainable parameters: ~145M
Expected inference time: 2-4 seconds per 512×512 image
Target FID score: 20-30 on LAION validation set

## Core Infrastructure Requirements

### Zig Build System Configuration

Create `build.zig` to manage compilation, CUDA integration, and dependency management.

```zig
const std = @import("std");

pub fn build(b: *std.Build) void {
    const target = b.standardTargetOptions(.{});
    const optimize = b.standardOptimizeOption(.{});

    // CUDA compilation settings
    const cuda_path = b.option([]const u8, "cuda-path", "Path to CUDA installation") orelse "/usr/local/cuda";

    // Main executable
    const exe = b.addExecutable(.{
        .name = "text-to-image",
        .root_source_file = .{ .path = "src/main.zig" },
        .target = target,
        .optimize = optimize,
    });

    // Link CUDA libraries
    exe.addLibraryPath(.{ .path = b.fmt("{s}/lib64", .{cuda_path}) });
    exe.addIncludePath(.{ .path = b.fmt("{s}/include", .{cuda_path}) });
    exe.linkSystemLibrary("cuda");
    exe.linkSystemLibrary("cudart");
    exe.linkSystemLibrary("cublas");
    exe.linkSystemLibrary("curand");
    exe.linkLibC();

    // Build CUDA kernels separately
    const cuda_kernels = b.addSystemCommand(&[_][]const u8{
        "nvcc",
        "-O3",
        "-arch=sm_90", // B200 architecture
        "-c",
        "src/cuda/kernels.cu",
        "-o",
        "cuda_kernels.o",
    });

    exe.addObjectFile(.{ .path = "cuda_kernels.o" });
    exe.step.dependOn(&cuda_kernels.step);

    b.installArtifact(exe);

    // Training executable
    const train_exe = b.addExecutable(.{
        .name = "train",
        .root_source_file = .{ .path = "src/train.zig" },
        .target = target,
        .optimize = optimize,
    });
    train_exe.addLibraryPath(.{ .path = b.fmt("{s}/lib64", .{cuda_path}) });
    train_exe.addIncludePath(.{ .path = b.fmt("{s}/include", .{cuda_path}) });
    train_exe.linkSystemLibrary("cuda");
    train_exe.linkSystemLibrary("cudart");
    train_exe.linkSystemLibrary("cublas");
    train_exe.linkSystemLibrary("curand");
    train_exe.linkLibC();
    train_exe.addObjectFile(.{ .path = "cuda_kernels.o" });
    train_exe.step.dependOn(&cuda_kernels.step);

    b.installArtifact(train_exe);
}
